# shellcheck shell=sh disable=SC2034
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  SLOBODA — operator config (sample)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  ⚠  HONESTY: this configures the NON-ATTESTABLE Android escape hatch —
#     "Postern for postmarketOS — community edition". It is NOT "Porog" (the
#     stock-Android container) and NOT "Postern OS". Entering Android = data
#     leaves the sealed base; Play Integrity STRONG fails (banking/Wallet/DRM
#     refuse); NOT covered by the Postern Seal; UNTESTED scaffold (no Waydroid
#     in the build sandbox). Not legal advice.
#
#  Copy to one of (first match wins):
#     ~/.config/sloboda/sloboda.conf
#     /etc/sloboda/sloboda.conf
#  It is sourced as POSIX sh (KEY=VALUE). Anything you don't set keeps the
#  private, default-safe value baked into the wrapper.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# --- Image system type: the microG-vs-GApps choice. A CONFIG INPUT, not a
#     hardcode. Default is the PRIVATE, Google-free base.
#       VANILLA  AOSP, no Google, no microG           (default, most private)
#       FOSS     microG-preinstalled image            (upstream images flaky)
#       GAPPS    Google Play Services                 (EXPLICIT, less private)
PAW_SYSTEM_TYPE=VANILLA

# --- Optionally run the community microG installer (waydroid_script) AFTER a
#     VANILLA init. 0 = leave it Google-free-and-serviceless. This is a
#     documented manual step, not automated here.
PAW_MICROG=0

# --- App-store-first landing package. Aurora Store is account-free delivery
#     (does NOT defeat Play Integrity). Swap for org.fdroid.fdroid, etc.
PAW_STORE_PKG=com.aurora.store

# --- Readiness polling.
PAW_READY_TIMEOUT=90
PAW_READY_INTERVAL=2

# --- Where host .desktop launchers are written.
#       Per-user (default): $XDG_DATA_HOME/applications — user-writable, NO root.
#       System-wide:        /usr/share/applications — needs root/packager; that is
#                           the NixOS module's job, not the wrapper's. Point this
#                           there ONLY from the packaged/rooted context; the
#                           wrapper fails honestly if it cannot write.
#     After writing/pruning, `sloboda launchers` best-effort runs
#     `update-desktop-database` so a live shell grid (Phosh) re-indexes promptly.
# PAW_DESKTOP_DIR=/usr/share/applications

# --- install-watch polling loop (`sloboda install-watch`). No install-event API
#     exists upstream, so launchers are kept in sync by polling `waydroid app
#     list` on an interval. PAW_WATCH_ONCE=1 makes it a single bounded pass
#     (cron-style / one-shot); the default long-runs until stopped.
PAW_WATCH_INTERVAL=15
# PAW_WATCH_ONCE=0

# --- Consent-gate privacy-bridge state file. OWNED BY THE CONSENT-GATE
#     COMPONENT. This wrapper only READS it and treats anything but a first line
#     of exactly "enabled" as OFF. Do NOT point this at a file this wrapper can
#     write — the whole point is that the wrapper cannot open the bridge itself.
# PAW_BRIDGE_STATE=/run/postern/consent/sloboda-bridge.state
